QuestGuidance.Register("en",11,{
[321]="70025B6C\n1\tDefeat Angmarim at Tham Ornen (total: 8)\tTham Ornen is north-east of Tinnudir. Brogdagnir implored to you to deliver a resounding defeat to the Angmarim encamped at Tham Ornen.\n2\tTalk to Brogdagnir at Tinnudir\tBrogdagnir is at Tinnudir, south-west of Tham Ornen. Brogdagnir will be pleased to hear that the Angmarim have been driven from Tham Ornen.\n",
[322]="7002EF0B\n1\tTalk to Léofrun\t\n2\tTalk to Léofrun\tLéofrun is hiding near a burnt tree in Thornhope. You should escort Léofrun to safety.\n3\tTalk to Léofrun at Béortnoth's camp\tLéofrun is at Béortnoth's camp, outside of Thornhope. You should speak with Léofrun when you return to Béortnoth's camp.\n",
[323]="700515FA\n1\tHelp hobbits celebrate in the spirit of the Harvest Festival (total: 6)\tSpiritless hobbits can be found throughout Wistmead. Walaric Goldworthy is concerned that hobbits visiting Wistmead are not celebrating in the proper spirit of the Harvest Festival. You should help them.\n2\tTalk to Walaric Goldworthy\tWalaric Goldworthy can be found in Wistmead. You have helped many hobbits rediscover the spirit of the Harvest Festival. You should return to Walaric Goldworthy.\n",
[324]="7002733D\n1\tTalk to Elladan in Tûr Morva\030Talk to Elrohir in Tûr Morva\tElladan is south of the Brenin's house, by the ruins of the ancient fort near Tûr Morva. Elrohir is on a small rise overlooking the lake, west of the entrance to Tûr Morva. Evan wants you to ask Elladan and Elrohir what they know about Dunland. He thinks they, and all Elves, look down on the shorter-lived races.\n2\tTalk to Evan in Tûr Morva\tEvan is just inside the entrance to Tûr Morva. You have spoken with Elladan and Elrohir concerning their knowledge of Dunlending history and should now report it to Evan. You may wish to be tactful.\n3\tTalk to Penrod in Tûr Morva\tPenrod is among the northern buildings of Tûr Morva. Evan has decided he is not as angry about Elves as he once was and wants you to tell Penrod.\n",
[325]="70071600\n1\tDefeat the restless trees near Shádhag (total: 12)\030Gather wood from the fallen trees (total: 12)\tDefeat marauding Huorns and gather cords of wood from the malevolent trees near Shádhag. Shádhag can be found north-west of Sormedân.\n2\tReturn to Elder Jurmêna in Sormedân with the wood\tReturn to Elder Jurmêna in Sormedân with the cords of wood.\n",
[326]="7002EB19\n1\tTalk to Heburga, daughter of the Thane\tHeburga is in the centre of Langhold, surrounded by a number of admiring children. You should speak with Heburga to find out about brigand-bashing. NOTE: This quest is solo-only, and cannot be completed in a fellowship.\n2\tPlay a game of Brigand-bashing with the children of Langhold\tThe children of Langhold have invited you to play a game of Brigand-bashing. You should speak with Heburga to join the children in their game. NOTE: This quest is solo-only, and cannot be completed in a fellowship.\n3\tTalk to Dala\tDala is at the north gate of Langhold. You should speak with Dala.\n",
[327]="7002F912\n1\tSearch the Orcs within the estate for the cellar key\tThe Orc with the cellar key is likely to be found inside of the estate that Cyneswith hides behind. Cyneswith has asked you to search for the cellar key among the Orcs pillaging within the estate.\n2\tReturn to Cyneswith near the cellar entrance\tCyneswith rests behind the estate, near the cellar door. You have found the cellar door's key and should return it to Cyneswith.\n3\tEnter the cellar of the farmhouse\tThe cellar door is located behind the estate, where Cyneswith waits. With the cellar door unlocked, you may now enter to search for Sager.\n4\tFind Cyneswith's son, Sager, in the cellar of the farmhouse\tYou should search for Sager within the cellar of the estate. You have entered the cellar of the estate and may begin searching for Sager, hopefully before the Orcs discover him.\n5\tReturn to Cyneswith outside the farmhouse\tCyneswith and Sager await your return on the outside of the estate. Sager has returned to his father's side. Cyneswith will be eager to see that you have rescued his son.\n",
[328]="70009C05\n1\tTake a red stick from the field\tThe red sticks are on the field. Haggo Boffin, the Captain of the Flying Feathers, has asked you to gather a red stick from the field and get ready to begin.\n2\tPlay a game of Hobnanigans\tScore as many goals as you can within the allotted time. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[329]="7003ED50\n1\tTake a red stick from the field\tThe red sticks are on the field. Gorbulas Millstone, the Captain of the Flying Feathers, has asked you to gather a red stick from the field and get ready to begin.\n2\tPlay a game of Hobnanigans\tScore as many goals as you can within the allotted time. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[330]="7003ED52\n1\tTake a red stick from the field\tThe red sticks are on the field. Olo Knotwise, the Captain of the Flying Feathers, has asked you to gather a red stick from the field and get ready to begin.\n2\tPlay a game of Hobnanigans\tScore as many goals as you can within the allotted time. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[331]="7003ED55\n1\tTake a red stick from the field\tThe red sticks are on the field. Dimple Grubb, the Captain of the Flying Feathers, has asked you to gather a red stick from the field and get ready to begin.\n2\tPlay a game of Hobnanigans\tScore as many goals as you can within the allotted time. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[332]="70009C06\n1\tTake a blue stick from the field\tThe blue sticks are on the field. Carnelian Bracegirdle, the Captain of the Steel Beaks, has asked you to gather a blue stick from the field and then get ready to play.\n2\tPlay a game of Hobnanigans\tScore as many goals as you can within the allotted time. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[333]="7003ED51\n1\tTake a blue stick from the field\tThe blue sticks are on the field. May Tighfield, the Captain of the Steel Beaks, has asked you to gather a blue stick from the field and then get ready to play.\n2\tPlay a game of Hobnanigans\tScore as many goals as you can within the allotted time. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[334]="7003ED53\n1\tTake a blue stick from the field\tThe blue sticks are on the field. Belba Hardbottle, the Captain of the Steel Beaks, has asked you to gather a blue stick from the field and then get ready to play.\n2\tPlay a game of Hobnanigans\tScore as many goals as you can within the allotted time. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[335]="7003ED54\n1\tTake a blue stick from the field\tThe blue sticks are on the field. Melilot Toadfoot, the Captain of the Steel Beaks, has asked you to gather a blue stick from the field and then get ready to play.\n2\tPlay a game of Hobnanigans\tScore as many goals as you can within the allotted time. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[336]="7002C24F\n1\tFrom a hiding place, whistle at the nearby fisherman to scare him\tThe fishermen's camp can be found along the banks of the Anduin in Thinglad. You should sneak to the camp, crouch in some undergrowth nearby, and perform tricks to try to frighten away the men. NOTE: This quest uses emotes. You must target the intended recipient of the emote in order for quest emotes to work.\n2\tWait a few moments\tWait a few moments before continuing.\n3\tFrom a hiding place, mumble at the nearby fisherman to scare him\tThe fishermen's camp can be found along the banks of the Anduin in Thinglad. You should sneak to the camp, crouch in some undergrowth nearby, and perform tricks to try to frighten away the men. NOTE: This quest uses emotes. You must target the intended recipient of the emote in order for quest emotes to work.\n4\tWait a few moments\tWait a few moments before trying again.\n5\tFrom a hiding place, roar at the nearby fisherman to scare him\tThe fishermen's camp can be found along the banks of the Anduin in Thinglad. You should sneak to the camp, crouch in some undergrowth nearby, and perform tricks to try to frighten away the men. NOTE: This quest uses emotes. You must target the intended recipient of the emote in order for quest emotes to work.\n6\tWait a few moments\tWait a few moments before trying again.\n7\tFrom a hiding place, clap at the nearby fisherman to scare him\tThe fishermen's camp can be found along the banks of the Anduin in Thinglad. You should sneak to the camp, crouch in some undergrowth nearby, and perform tricks to try to frighten away the men. NOTE: This quest uses emotes. You must target the intended recipient of the emote in order for quest emotes to work.\n8\tFind the Elf-outpost of Haldirith\tNoriel has retreated to the Elf-ruins of Haldirith in Thinglad, at the centre of the forest, upon a hill. You should speak with Noriel.\n",
[337]="7002616A\n1\tCollect cherry wood branches (total: 8)\tCherry wood branches can be found in the fields south of Duillond along the road to Celondim, probably near the bases of trees. You should collect cherry wood for the reinforcement of the soles in the Shrew-stomping boots.\n2\tBring the cherry wood branches to Deluraw\tDeluraw can be found in Duillond near the ovens. You should bring the cherry wood branches you collected to Deluraw.\n",
[338]="7005783D\n1\tDefeat Hregmód, if that is his name\tA terrible stone-giant walks among the hills of Misthallow. Rumour says that he is called Hregmód, and ending this creature would bring some amount of peace throughout the region.\n2\tDefeat Hregmód, if that is his name\tSearch among the hills of Misthallow, and see if you can find the creature called Hregmód. Be wary none can remember who might have given him that name, as no one to see him up close has survived.\n3\tCompleted\tCompleted.\n",
[339]="70020DBC\n1\tDefeat Gavar-diavol at night\tGavar-diavol can be found at night in a gully south of Rhus Cornchúthur. Rhus Cornchúthur suggested you rid the Gloomglens of the Druggavar called Gavar-diavol. Doing so may go a long way to building a friendship with the hobbits of Enedwaith.\n2\tTalk to Rhus Cornchúthur in the Gloomglens\tRhus Cornchúthur awaits your return to the west of Gavar-diavol's haunting grounds. You should return to Rhus Cornchúthur with news of your victory.\n",
[340]="70043B72\n1\tWait for Radagast\tRadagast can be found in Rhosgobel. Wait for Radagast to find what he is looking for.\n2\tTalk to Radagast\tRadagast can be found in Rhosgobel. You should talk to Radagast.\n",
[341]="70045286\n1\tLook for Sithgar\tLook for a young rider named Sithgar in Ost Rimmon, in the Beacon Hills.\n2\tHelp Sithgar\tYou should help Sithgar recover his horse and return to his Éored.\n3\tReturn to Guthláf\tWhen you return to the Rohirrim bivouac, you should let Guthláf know that you found Sithgar in Ost Rimmon and helped him to ready his horse for travel again.\n",
[342]="70022929\n1\tMake sure that Amdir drinks the bilberry tea\tAmdir sits across the lane from Celandine, in the centre of Archet. You should bring Celandine's restorative bilberry tea to Amdir to help him gather his strength and wits.\n2\tReturn to Celandine and lie for Amdir's sake\tCelandine is across the lane from Amdir, in Archet's centre. You should return to Celandine and lie to her on Amdir's behalf. He did not drink her tea, but he does not wish her to be disappointed....\n",
[343]="70002E5C\n1\tBring Arrod's necklace to Narlinn\tNarlinn is at Thorenhad, the camp of the sons of Elrond located among the Bruinen Gorges, north of the bear dens. Arrod has asked you to deliver the necklace to Narlinn, the Elf-maid who is the object of his devotion.\n2\tBring Arrod's necklace back to Arrod\tArrod is at his vantage point high above the Bruinen Gorges, by an old set of ruins. Narlinn has refused Arrod's gift and has sent you to return it to him.\n",
[344]="70071B2C\n1\tTalk to Mêshaget\tGôbezhir has asked you to talk to Mêshaget and see if he will join the two of you. Mêshaget is in the courtyard of Jiret-menêsh.\n2\tReturn to Gôbezhir\tYou have invited Mêshaget to join you and Gôbezhir, so that the two of you can present him with a gift. Gôbezhir is in the crafting area of Jiret-menêsh.\n3\tComplete Instance: A Gift for the Future\tYou have invited Mêshaget to join you and Gôbezhir, so that the two of you can present him with a gift.\n4\tTalk to Gôbezhir\tYou went with Gôbezhir to present his masterwork axe to Mêshaget.\n",
[345]="7004CE43\n1\tTalk to Mervárth\tMervárth can be found in the Trade Commission Headquarters in Lake-town. You should talk to Mervárth.\n2\tTalk to Eigár the Dock-worker\tEigár can be found in Lake-town. You should talk to Eigár.\n3\tTalk to Víthog the Forester\tVíthog the Forester can be found in the Dale-lands west of Lake-town. You should talk to Víthog the Forester.\n4\tTry to find an appropriate piece of wood (quantity: see journal)\tThe scrap pile can be found near the forester's house. You should search the scrap pile for a good piece of wood.\n5\tTalk to Málmi in Erebor, in the Hall Under the Mountain\tMálmi the Ore Trader can be found in Erebor, in the Hall Under the Mountain. You should talk to Málmi.\n6\tCollect copper ore\030Collect calamine ore\tCopper and calamine ore can be found nearby in Erebor. You should collect a chunk of copper ore and a chunk of calamine ore.\n7\tTalk to Málmi\tMálmi the Ore Trader can be found in Erebor. You should talk to Málmi.\n8\tTalk to Rísta\tRísta can be found in Dale. You should talk to Rísta.\n9\tTalk to Dagrun\tDagrun can be found in the Master's manor in Lake-town. You should talk to Dagrun.\n",
[346]="70000DE9\n1\tSpeak to Ulfar\tOlwir's camp is in the northern reaches of Rushock Bog. Ulfar has decided that Olwir's plan must be put to an end and has asked you to gather a party of warriors to accompany him to the camp. Once there, he plans to inflitrate the camp and slay any Stone-troll Olwir's dwarves may have captured.\n2\tTalk to Ulfar\tUlfar is back in Needlehole. Having succeeded in your quest, you should return to Ulfar to tell him what happened.\n",
[347]="7006E4C5\n1\tApproach the gate\tYou must find a way to enter the dwarf camp.\n2\tChallenge the Dourhands at the gate\tYou must find a way to enter the dwarf camp. Perhaps challenging the dwarves to combat will get them to open the gate.\n3\tChallenge the Dourhands at the gate\tYou must find a way to enter the dwarf camp.\n4\tWait for the Dourhands\tThe Dourhands have opened the gate to answer your challenge.\n5\tSlap the Dourhand tracker\tThe Dourhands have opened the gate to answer your challenge. You should do something that will initiate combat.\n6\tSearch the camp for Olwir\tYou have defeated the dwarves guarding the gate. You should proceed into the camp in search of Olwir or a Stone-troll.\n7\tDefeat Olwir's guards\tYou have found Olwir, and he has a caged Stone-troll! You should defeat the Dourhands protecting him.\n8\tConfront Olwir\tYou have found Olwir, and defeated the guards protecting him. He has a caged Stone-troll! You should confront Olwir.\n9\tDefeat the Stone-troll\tIt appears that Olwir is no longer a problem, but now you have a bigger one - a Strone-troll that must be defeated.\n",
[348]="7002FE89\n1\tGather well-prepared food (total: 4)\030Gather freshly-harvested grain (total: 4)\030Collect Fastred's pendant\tFood can be found in the Mead Hall and kitchens throughout Snowbourn. Grain can be found in the fields directly outside town. Fastred's pendant can be found in his home. Fastred wants you to help him prepare a gift of sorts to be sent to Edoras. He wishes for you to gather some portions of the gift while he handles his own preparations.\n2\tLoad Fastred's steed with the gifts\tHaving gathered your portion of Fastred's gift, you should load it onto the horse he mentioned earlier. The horse can be found outside the mead-hall.\n3\tTalk to Fastred\tFastred can be found in the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.\n",
[349]="7004744E\n1\tScrape moss from sun-touched Morgul-trolls in North Ithilien (total: 9)\tSun-touched Morgul-trolls can be found in the hills surrounding Henneth Annûn. Ereblen has asked you to return to the sun-touched Morgul-trolls you found previously and scrape patches of moss from them.\n2\tDeliver the moss to Ereblen in Henneth Annûn\tEreblen can be found in Henneth Annûn. You have gathered a suitable amount of moss from the sun-touched trolls and should now deliver it to Ereblen.\n",
[350]="7006C577\n1\tFill the phial with oasis water near the three sister trees\030Get near enough to the oasis to fill the phial\tTharashil gave you an empty phial and sent you to the oasis, near the three sister trees, to collect water. She then told you to visit Aítarshun and Filadal. She suggested they would know what to do once you explained why you were there.\n2\tAllow Aítarshun to examine the oasis water\030Allow Filadal to examine the oasis water\tYou filled the phial with Shonith oasis water. Visit Aítarshun and Filadal and tell them why Tharashil sent you. Tharashil stated they will understand what they need to do.\n3\tAllow Tharashil to examine the oasis water\tAítarshun and Filadal both held the water and spoke words. You do not understand the meaning or the ritual, but both seem to believe this will aid the Men of Khûd Zagin in a time of need. Return the water to Tharashil.\n4\tDeliver the gift from Shonith to Amalíbi at Ghalburu\tTharashil returned the water to you with a warning and instruction. You are to deliver the water to Amalíbi. Tharashil does not believe Amalíbi will understand the value but believes in time she will.\n",
[351]="70071CCB\n1\tPick up the cheese deliveries from Majâryan's table (total: 3)\tPick up the cheese deliveries from Majâryan's table in the Court of Larinâsta in Zajâna.\n2\tDeliver the first cheese basket to the first customer\030Deliver the second cheese basket to the second customer\030Deliver the third cheese basket to the third customer\tDeliver the cheese baskets to each of three customers in Zajâna.\n3\tSpeak with Majâryan in the Court of Larinâsta\tReturn to the Court of Larinâsta in Zajâna and speak with Majâryan.\n",
[352]="7001A63C\n1\tTalk to Menassiel at Cerin Amroth\tMenassiel can be found at Cerin Amroth in Lothlórien. You should speak with Menassiel and see if she will gift the Huorns of Mirkwood with a young mallorn, a light to dispel the shadows upon their wretched existence.\n2\tBring the mallorn sapling to Nífdir\tNífdir is at his camp in the Drownholt, west of the Malledhrim outpost of Estolad Mernael. You should return to Nífdir to show him the seedling donated by Menassiel.\n",
})
